this video is sponsored by bok su no  other character represents the moral  landscape of the one piece world  as well as monkey d garp the hero  of the marines as the father of the most  wanted person in the world as well as  the grandfather of the future pirate  king and the son of the old one  garp without any doubt plays a quite  unique role in the story  especially given the fact that he's one  of the most respected members within the  marines  the sworn enemy of pirates and  revolutionaries alike  [Music]  and yet the two defining traits of his  character max to his kind-hearted and  goofy nature  are his strong sense of duty as well as  his love for his criminal family  and as we will see it is exactly this  stark polarization of beliefs that makes  him such a tragic  and lovable person this is the story of  monkey d  garden  [Music]  garb is mostly known for two feats the  defeat of the rox pirates on god valley  as well as the capture of gold d roger  even though garp has enjoyed immense  respect and special treatment within the  marines for them  both of these events have actually been  doctored as we now know  roger actually handed himself in  willingly to trigger the next pirate era  meanwhile he actually fought side by  side with garb to defeat rox  which makes it very hard to assess how  strong  he truly is  since he was able to fight with some of  the most powerful beings in the one  piece world however  and was offered the position of admiral  multiple times  it's pretty safe to assume that garb is  very much the real deal  from a storytelling perspective garb  actually has a quite unique character  design  or to put it in better terms he doesn't  seem to fit in  any traditional trope or category even  though he's the grandfather to both  luffy and ace and was the one who  trained them both  he doesn't really fit the trope of the  classical old man mentor  that role falls to rayleigh for luffy  and to whitebeard for ace  a better fit might be that of a parental  figure that he  clearly is to both of the boys however  while he showered both of them with  tough love  he also didn't exactly stick around all  too much as well  in the end i believe that garp is  several important supporting characters  mashed into one for example he  represents the old era from the marines  perspective  that includes other legends like roger  or whitebeard  he is a father figure to the main  character balanced in such a way that  luffy has experienced both  love and care in his childhoods while  still benefiting from the classical  shonen hero without parents trope that  gives him independence and drive  kind of ironic actually that luffy  mostly grew up an orphan  even though he has both an actual father  and grandfather who are both still alive  and well  the biggest role that garth plays in the  story however is that he represents the  blurred moral lines between the  different groups  operating in the one piece worlds like  no other as we all know the notion that  all marines are good  and all pirates are evil is pretty much  thrown out the window within the first  few chapters  instead we learn that there are good  marines and bad marines just as there  are good pirates and bad pirates  and of course a ton of people who fall  somewhere in between  for example we know that the marines who  claim to be fighting for peace and  justice  also serve at the will of the celestial  dragons a tyrannical regime of hedonic  slave owners  at the same time while a lot of pirates  simply seek freedom from this regime of  oppression  many are just as terrible on the other  end of the table  killing and terrorizing the innocent  civilians who are  helplessly caught between both fronts  and so monkey d-garp is the  personification of the question  what does it mean to be good this is  actually a quite  interesting theme within the monkey  family while luffy literally values  family above all  else as we see with his crew or with ace  and  rejects any sense of duty to any system  his father dragon on the other hand  ended up putting duty above all else  even if it meant  abandoning his own child garp meanwhile  is  literally torn between both duty and  family  looking for a way to balance them not  always successfully  in the end what all three of them desire  is freedom and a just world  free of the terror of the celestial  dragons but also from  pirates like blackbeard or doflamingo  however based on each of their ideals  luffy chose the path of piracy  dragon that of the revolutionary and  garb that of the marine  and while luffy represents the best  within the world of pirates  garp very clearly embodies the best  within the marines  his approach to justice i've actually  talked about that of the four marine  admirals as well  is by far the most human and relatable  making him the flagship of that type of  marine  that we as an audience want to see and  that in the future will likely end up  becoming the new normal this includes  people like smoker or aokiji who see him  as a role model  but also a line of young marines like  kobe  who garb chose and trained himself  i would actually argue then that garb as  a member of the d-clan and the notorious  monkey family  is the one who is quietly nursing a more  just and independent generation of  marines  with the freedom and desire to actually  work for and protect the people  and not the celestial dragons before we  move on to the tragic part of garp's  character however let's  first lighten the mood a bit as you may  or may not know  it's finally the long-awaited sakura  season here in japan  and to celebrate the occasion the kind  folks over at box zoo sent me  this wonderful snack box boxu is a  monthly snack box subscription service  that delivers original assortments of  premium japanese snacks and tea pairings  directly from japan to wherever you live  and as i get it there is a different  theme for every season  and since i love hanami i got lucky and  got the sakura one so  let's open this bad boy up and see  what's inside because i absolutely love  the snacks here in japan  i love the bubble wrap  how cute is that i actually love this so  it does  come with a description of all the  contents  of the box itself this here is the green  tea what i really like about this  is that they collaborate with  traditional japanese family  manufacturers that make these snacks and  candies  so you don't just get some random stuff  you can also get in any japanese  supermarket  but actual local stuff i think  especially when you're outside of japan  this  is a great opportunity to try some real  authentic japanese food  try this monaco because it actually  looks really good  looks like uh this  [Music]  this is sakura cake if you would like to  try it out for yourself you can get 10  of your own boxes snack box and save up  to 47 bucks using my  code and links in description below  and this brings us back to the tragedy  of garp's character his inner divide  between  love towards his family and duty towards  the organization that he believes will  bring justice to the world  we can see this divide very clearly in  the fact that garp has a very  interesting approach to dealing with  pirates which is  judging them based on their actions and  their personality as  he is well aware of the dark system  overshadowing the marines as well we  know this because garb  doesn't actually make a secret out of  his disdain for the world nobles  in fact the only reason he never  accepted any promotion above vice  admiral  was because the positions of fleet  admiral and admiral are under the direct  command of the world governments  as a result similar to smoker and luffy  he started to build an actual  relationship with roger after chasing  him for so many years  in the end their relationship was of  such mutual respect and understanding  that they not only fought together  roger actually entrusted garb with his  precious child  telling him that he trusted him as much  as his crew which  let's be honest is a real goosebump  moment  whether he also told garb about his  plans and the knowledge he found on love  tale  remains to be seen but garb was willing  to accept his old rival's request and  took ace in  anyway garp in turn entrusts ace to  dardan and then some time later luffy as  well  occasionally paying them visits and  hoping to shape them into future marines  each of them has their own reason to  become a pirate and disobey him but  this doesn't change the fact that they  are family and so he continues to pour  his love onto them albeit through fists  of love  and garb wanting ace and luffy to become  marines shows us just how much he  actually respects his job  no doubt hoping to make his voice part  of this new generation  and yet despite these expectations he  keeps laughing whenever he hears about  luffy's exploits in the worlds  even when the marines are directly  involved and so it's no real surprise  that marine fort was not only the climax  for luffy's character arc so far  but of garbs as well when he sits next  to his grandson who is about to be  executed  there was not a hint of a smile  garp instead cries cries not only in  sorrow of seeing his grandson in such a  situation  but also cries because of his inability  to do anything about it  his life as a marine has tied his hands  completely  in the end garp decides to choose duty  over family  as he takes down marco who had no issues  dealing with the other admirals so far  he boosts the morale of the marines and  then just  moments later he has to witness luffy  his second grandson  running towards him the ultimate dilemma  now he was standing in the way of one  grandson rescuing his other grandson  and so in this moment of turmoil as he  sees his happy days with the boys pass  before his eyes  he gives himself up and allows luffy to  punch him and pass  [Music]  and so i believe that the true reason  garp is so incredibly enraged at a kainu  killing ace is that right from the start  he never  actually thought that ace was going to  be executed  instead he fully expected that  whitebeard and his crew and later luffy  would save ace as a result we got one of  the most emotional and heartbreaking  scenes in the story as sengoku has to  restrain himself from murdering akainu  and the same goes for his reaction to  shanks arriving who was responsible for  setting luffy  on the same path as ace and so on this  day  garb the marine won but garb the man  lost now i personally would like to  believe that garb will have the chance  to choose again at some point in the  future  to save his other grandson or stay loyal  to the marines  and this time he will choose family over  duty if you want to watch more of my  character analyses you can simply click  up here or if you want to see my latest  video down  there thanks for watching peace
 

